\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 PART 1: Product Vision & Core Philosophy\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf0 1.1 The Objective\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 The eXp India Prestige Portal is a structured, performance-based upskilling and learning framework. It is a behavioral motivation system designed to guide associates from 'Unbranded & Invisible' to 'Multi-Channel Digital Leaders'. It provides total transparency into their career roadmap and the tangible rewards they unlock by advancing .\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2 \cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 1.2 Strict Terminology & Identity Rules\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0
\fs24 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The User:
\f1\b0  Must strictly be referred to as an 
\f0\b 'Associate'
\f1\b0 . The word 'Agent' is completely forbidden in the UI and must only exist in backend data keys if required by the database.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The Tiers:
\f1\b0  Progress levels are 
\f0\b 'Milestone Badges'
\f1\b0  (e.g., Bronze Badge, Silver Badge).\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 \uc0\u8232 
\f0\b Identity Hierarchy:
\f1\b0  The UI header must prominently and distinctly separate the Associate's 
\f0\b Honor Title
\f1\b0  (their operational role, e.g., Business Associate) from their 
\f0\b Milestone Badge
\f1\b0  (their pathway progress). \uc0\u8232 \u8232 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 1.3 The Support Philosophy\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Progress is performance-based, not time-based. The dashboard must reflect that eXp India's support model evolves as the associate ranks up: from "we build you" (Entry) and "we work for you" (Bronze/Silver), to "we work alongside you" (Gold), and finally "we partner with you" (Diamond).\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2 \cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1 \cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 PART 2: Technical Architecture & Security (Decoupled System)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 To protect the integrity of the Master Google Sheet and bypass browser-level authentication conflicts (e.g., Google Apps Script multi-login failures), the portal utilizes a strictly decoupled Read/Write architecture.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 2.1 The "Read" Layer (Public & Safe API)\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0
\fs24 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Mechanism:
\f1\b0  The Vercel frontend uses a restricted Google Sheets API key to fetch data.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls5\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Target Database:
\f1\b0  The main tab named exactly Agents_Master.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls6\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Security:
\f1\b0  The API key is restricted to "View Only." The Vercel app cannot write, delete, or alter any data in the Master Sheet under any circumstances.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 2.2 The "Write" Layer (Webhook Middleware)\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls7\ilvl0
\fs24 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Mechanism:
\f1\b0  When an Associate submits an assignment/proof, the Vercel app uses a standard JavaScript fetch() to POST a JSON payload to a secure Webhook URL (e.g., Make.com or Zapier).\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls8\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Data Payload:
\f1\b0  The JSON must include: \{ timestamp, associateName, associateId, currentBadge, pillar, taskName, proofUrl, notes \}.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls9\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
